!  Parameters for the alpha functions of the cubic equations of state.
!
!  Numerical parameters from Mahmoodi and Sedigh, Fluid Phase Equilibria,
!  doi 10.1016/j.fluid.2016.12.015. The columns hold fitted coefficients for
!  the model presented there, for Soave-Redlich-Kwong and Peng-Robinson.
!
!  The coefficients are fitted numerical results, not a collected compilation.
!  BELFEM can use a row only when its CAS number matches a species in gasdata.inp
!  and that species is reachable by the gas-table reader. This reachability
!  criterion comes from BELFEM, so the selection and ordering below do not follow
!  an external table.
!
!  If a species has no entry here, BELFEM falls back to the Coquelet, Chapoy and
!  Richon correlation, doi 10.1023/B:IJOT.0000022331.46865.2f, which needs only
!  the acentric factor.
!
!  Lookup uses the CAS number in column two.
!
!  The C3H6 row is cyclopropane (CAS 75-19-4), not propylene (115-07-1).
!
!  pH2 (para-hydrogen) and He3 (helium-3) are carried for the cryogenic range.
!  Para-hydrogen has no CAS registry number of its own; 1333-74-0p follows the
!  CoolProp convention. Both rows are inert until gasdata.inp and thermo.inp
!  carry the species.
!
